# NOTE: git does NOT support trailing comments on a pattern line — the whole
# line, comment included, is taken as the pattern. Every comment here is on its
# own line for that reason. (An earlier version wrote
# `data/cache/   # 245 MB of tensors`, which silently ignored nothing and got a
# 164 MB file committed, which GitHub then rejected at push time.)

# Derived artefacts — regenerate with `python scripts/train.py`
# data/cache is ~245 MB of rendered tensors and is pure cache.
data/cache/

# Resumable-training scratch files.
models/checkpoint.keras
models/best.keras
models/train_state.json

# Deliberately NOT ignored, because the app or the submission needs them:
#   models/fallguard_cnn.npz    the app cannot run without it (0.8 MB)
#   models/labels.json          serving metadata
#   models/fallguard_cnn.keras  archival Keras copy (2.4 MB)
#   reports/                    evaluation evidence, incl. prediction panels
#   data/fallguard_dataset.npz  the corpus itself (6.7 MB), keeps results reproducible

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.DS_Store

*.mp4
!assets/*.mp4

.streamlit/secrets.toml
